== B2. Weak-field gravitomagnetic counterflow estimate (OURS, order of magnitude) ==
  Linearised GR: a mass current with momentum P on a shell of radius R gives a uniform interior
  h_0i = 4 G P/(c^3 R). Counterflowing +P at R1 and -P at R2 gives interior beta = (4G P/c^3)(1/R1 - 1/R2)
  with zero net exterior momentum. Momentum is bounded by energy: c P <= E_flow (DEC, u -> c).
  beta=0.02, R1=10, R2=20 m: E_flow,min = 1.210e+43 J = 1.347e+26 kg-equiv = 7.095e-02 M_J; at u=0.1c needs mass 1.347e+27 kg; at u=10 km/s needs 4.037e+30 kg
  beta=0.04, R1=10, R2=20 m: E_flow,min = 2.421e+43 J = 2.693e+26 kg-equiv = 1.419e-01 M_J; at u=0.1c needs mass 2.693e+27 kg; at u=10 km/s needs 8.074e+30 kg
  beta=0.02, R1=100, R2=200 m: E_flow,min = 1.210e+44 J = 1.347e+27 kg-equiv = 7.095e-01 M_J; at u=0.1c needs mass 1.347e+28 kg; at u=10 km/s needs 4.037e+31 kg
  beta=1e-06, R1=10, R2=20 m: E_flow,min = 6.051e+38 J = 6.733e+21 kg-equiv = 3.547e-06 M_J; at u=0.1c needs mass 6.733e+22 kg; at u=10 km/s needs 2.018e+26 kg
  published shell: E_flow,min / (M c^2) = 0.030  -> effective counterflow speed ~ 0.030 c if half the mass flows each way
  law: beta ~ (2G E_flow/(c^4 R1)) for R2 = 2 R1, i.e. beta ~ compactness x (u/c). Gap shrinks linearly in beta and R1.

